# onopen scanning onopen.
#
# tests/fixtures/trapped/ is a repository built to be hostile: every finding in
# it is deliberate and is what the test suite asserts on. Silencing the fixtures
# is the honest reading — they are test data, not configuration this repository
# runs. The rest of the tree stays under the scanner, so a real execution path
# added to onopen itself still fails the build.
*  tests/fixtures/**
